# [[.ProjectName]]

This repository was bootstrapped with the
[FiftyTen Golden Path](https://github.com/5010-dev/.github/blob/main/docs/guides/bootstrap-new-repository.md).

## Initial repository flow

For an empty remote, seed a common empty root and create the bootstrap work branch before
validation. Staging the generated tree lets `just check` inspect whitespace without committing
unvalidated files:

```bash
git init -b main
git commit --allow-empty -m "chore: initialize repository"
git branch dev
git switch dev
git switch -c chore/bootstrap-golden-path
git add .
```

## Development setup

Install [Mise](https://mise.jdx.dev/installing-mise.html) through a supported package manager
(`brew install mise` on macOS), not a network-to-shell pipeline. Review `mise.toml`, `mise.lock`,
and `scripts/golden-path` before establishing trust, then prepare and validate the repository from
its root:

```bash
mise trust
mkdir -p .cache/golden-path/mise-config
: > .cache/golden-path/mise-config/global.toml
export MISE_CONFIG_DIR="$PWD/.cache/golden-path/mise-config"
export MISE_GLOBAL_CONFIG_FILE="$PWD/.cache/golden-path/mise-config/global.toml"
mise install --locked
mise exec -- just init
mise exec -- just ci
```

Use `mise exec -- just --list` to discover the repository's standard commands.
`mise exec -- just check` is the optional faster non-mutating check; `mise exec -- just ci` is the
complete repository quality gate also executed by GitHub Actions. Release and deployment commands
and documentation should be added only when this repository gains those real boundaries.

Routine dependency updates start paused at `open-pull-requests-limit: 0`. Classify actual native
roots against existing repository release units with `golden-path dependency preview` before
enabling a bounded routine budget. Do not create dummy release units or package mappings. Security
visibility and remediation remain independent from the routine pause.

## Contribution flow

Follow the organization
[contribution guide](https://github.com/5010-dev/.github/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md). Work starts
from `dev`; reviewed work branches merge back to `dev`, and validated releases promote from `dev` to
`main` by fast-forward.

After the bootstrap validation passes, commit the reviewed tree and submit the first pull request to
`dev`:

```bash
git commit
git remote add origin <repository-url>
git push -u origin main
git push -u origin dev
git push -u origin chore/bootstrap-golden-path
mise exec -- gh pr create --base dev
```

After that pull request merges, validate `dev` and promote it to `main` with the fast-forward
procedure in the organization contribution guide.

## Generated ownership

Golden Path upgrades continue to manage only the request, metadata, managed-asset inventory,
conformance caller, and bootstrap script under `.github/` and `scripts/golden-path`. All other
generated files—including this README, source, manifests, locks, Just recipes, dependency policy,
CODEOWNERS, Dependabot configuration, and the repository quality workflow—are repository-owned scaffolding
and may be changed normally.
